  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Scarlet Begonias** (1 review): The Scarlet, Playing, Uncle John's Band, Fire on the Mountain sequence is singled out as especially inspired [4]\n- **Playing in the Band** (1 review): Reviewer found the Playing in the Band into Uncle John's Band stretch stellar [6]\n- **Drums** (1 other source): Oteil played drums during the Drums segment [1]\n- **Mickey** (1 other source): Oteil switched to bass for the Mickey segment [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Easy Wind**: rare: 14 archived performances [8]\n- **Box of Rain**: back after 62 archived shows (1082 days); rare: 11 archived performances [8]\n- **Mickey**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [8]\n- **Spanish Jam**: rare: 8 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dac2022-06-21.AKGmix.toaste.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 188 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **deadco2022-06-21**: source not stated; 18 songs; 188 min; rated 4/5 by 3 [2]. Said about its sound: Taper's recording is upfront and very clear, with all instruments well balanced [4]\n- **deadco2022-06-21.akg461-adktl-16bit**: source not stated; 18 songs; 189 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Very hot at the venue, about 97 degrees at 7pm; the reviewer was on the lawn [6]\n- Reviewer says it was the last show where Billy K. drummed the whole show [6]\n- Reviewer describes two guitarists, two drummers, a bassist and a keyboardist trading solos and building off each other [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dac2022-06-21.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: 3x AKG398 shotguns (L,C,R); 1x AKG394 Figure-8 (L,R); 2x AKG391 cardioids DIN (L,R); 2x AKG392 omnis 2-foot spread (L,R) > Zoom F8 @ 44.1/16 [1]. Also: Recorded with AKG shotgun, figure-8, cardioid and omni microphone pairs into a Zoom F8 at 44.1kHz/16-bit [1]\n- **deadco2022-06-21.akg461-adktl-16bit**: taped by jimmiec; transferred by jimmiec; source: AKG460 ck61 - ORTF, ADK TL hyper - PAS (Lawn, DFC) ~> DR-680 (24/48) [3]. Also: Mixed sources in Audacity, then CDWave, FLAC encoding, and Foobar2000 tagging, ending at 16/44.1 [3]",
